      "text": "Let $n$ be a two-digit number, which can be expressed as \\(10a + b\\), where \\(a\\) is the tens digit and \\(b\\) is the units digit. When we switch the digits, the new number becomes \\(10b + a\\).\n\nAccording to the problem, switching the digits and then adding 3 results in \\(2n\\). Therefore, we can set up the following equation:\n\\[\n10b + a + 3 = 2(10a + b)\n\\]\nExpanding the right side, we get:\n\\[\n10b + a + 3 = 20a + 2b\n\\]\nRearranging terms to isolate the variables on one side, we have:\n\\[\n10b + a + 3 = 20a + 2b \\implies 10b - 2b + a - 20a = -3 \\implies 8b - 19a = -3\n\\]\nWe need to find integer values for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) (where \\(a\\) is a digit from 1 to 9 and \\(b\\) is a digit from 0 to 9). Let's solve for \\(b\\) in terms of \\(a\\):\n\\[\n8b = 19a - 3 \\implies b = \\frac{19a - 3}{8}\n\\]\nFor \\(b\\) to be an integer, \\(19a - 3\\) must be divisible by 8. We can check the values of \\(a\\) to find a suitable \\(b\\):\n\n- If \\(a = 1\\), then \\(19 \\cdot 1 - 3 = 16\\), which is divisible by 8. So, \\(b = \\frac{16}{8} = 2\\). Therefore, \\(n = 10a + b = 10 \\cdot 1 + 2 = 12\\).\n- If \\(a = 2\\), then \\(19 \\cdot 2 - 3 = 35\\), which is not divisible by 8.\n- If \\(a = 3\\), then \\(19 \\cdot 3 - 3 = 54\\), which is not divisible by 8.\n- If \\(a = 4\\), then \\(19 \\cdot 4 - 3 = 77\\), which is not divisible by 8.\n- If \\(a = 5\\), then \\(19 \\cdot 5 - 3 = 98\\), which is not divisible by 8.\n- If \\(a = 6\\), then \\(19 \\cdot 6 - 3 = 119\\), which is not divisible by 8.\n- If \\(a = 7\\), then \\(19 \\cdot 7 - 3 = 140\\), which is divisible by 8. So, \\(b = \\frac{140}{8} = 17.5\\), which is not an integer.\n- If \\(a = 8\\), then \\(19 \\cdot 8 - 3 = 167\\), which is not divisible by 8.\n- If \\(a = 9\\), then \\(19 \\cdot 9 - 3 = 186\\), which is not divisible by 8.\n\nThe only valid solution is when \\(a = 1\\) and \\(b = 2\\), giving us \\(n = 12\\).\n\nThus, the smallest two-digit integer \\(n\\) that satisfies the condition is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).\n\nTo verify, we switch the digits of 12 to get 21, and then add 3 to get 24. Indeed, \\(2 \\cdot 12 = 24\\), so our solution is correct.",
